WEBVTT

00:00:05.170 --> 00:00:10.710
No more... I can't take it any more!

00:00:14.910 --> 00:00:17.490
We have no use for those who can't survive!

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:20.640
Be strong for Roland's sake!

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:23.540
That is the only reason you have to exist!

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:48.940
Idiot!

00:00:53.380 --> 00:00:54.650
Ryner...

00:00:54.650 --> 00:00:56.110
I'll beat the crap out of you!

00:00:57.200 --> 00:01:00.100
There are tons of people who want to live, but die anyway.

00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:02.150
Don't be so spoiled!

00:01:02.150 --> 00:01:07.200
But... I don't want to see it any more! Everyone dies...

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:11.260
I don't want to see it either.

00:01:11.860 --> 00:01:12.940
So...

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:35.090
Listen. Hold my hand tight, and never let go.

00:03:34.340 --> 00:03:37.490
Basically, this means there aren't any heroes' relics here.

00:03:38.990 --> 00:03:42.030
It's been said that there's something so well-hidden, they built this fortress to guard it.

00:03:42.030 --> 00:03:46.070
You'd think it would be a hero's relic, and yet...

00:03:46.710 --> 00:03:51.410
What they're hiding here are just records of tax evaders? You've got to be kidding me.

00:03:51.830 --> 00:03:54.230
I've gotten a general grasp of the situation.

00:03:55.290 --> 00:03:57.700
Well? Any last words?

00:03:58.620 --> 00:04:00.670
H-Hold on, wait a second!

00:04:02.470 --> 00:04:04.590
A place more likely to have a hero's relic...

00:04:11.480 --> 00:04:12.900
belonging to a hero recorded in literature.

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:15.030
And?

00:04:15.030 --> 00:04:16.310
And, uh...

00:04:16.310 --> 00:04:19.780
Remember the place where we camped yesterday? In the woods.

00:04:21.610 --> 00:04:26.700
To be honest, the map had an "X" marked right around that area...

00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:30.320
Oh? And you didn't tell me this?

00:04:30.320 --> 00:04:33.420
W-Well, if we couldn't spot the hero's sword,

00:04:33.420 --> 00:04:35.750
that would mean someone had drawn it already,

00:04:35.750 --> 00:04:37.060
or that it had gotten buried.

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:42.460
Digging up a relic from thousands of years ago would be a huge hassle.

00:04:42.460 --> 00:04:44.270
You didn't want to bother?

00:04:45.460 --> 00:04:48.680
That's why, uh... I'm sorry! See, uh...

00:04:48.680 --> 00:04:53.600
As for those who have been skulking around for the past few minutes, who are you?

00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:54.660
Yeah.

00:04:55.280 --> 00:04:57.270
If you're gonna attack, can't you just get it over with?

00:04:57.550 --> 00:04:59.600
Ah, jeez...

00:04:59.600 --> 00:05:03.340
Brother Sui, we were noticed because you kept shuffling around!

00:05:03.340 --> 00:05:04.970
Eh? It's my fault?

00:05:04.970 --> 00:05:08.570
Of course it is! Jeez, jeez, jeez!

00:05:09.820 --> 00:05:12.240
All right, the treasure's right in front of us.

00:05:12.570 --> 00:05:16.100
Our opposition looks tough, so be ready to flee at any time.

00:05:21.070 --> 00:05:24.740
Oh, brother Sui, you've turned 26 and still can't earn a living!

00:05:24.950 --> 00:05:28.790
This poor 14-year-old keeps looking after an artist who does nothing but dream,

00:05:28.790 --> 00:05:34.820
unable to fall in love, unable to get married, just wasting away!

00:05:34.820 --> 00:05:36.640
Well, that's a problem.

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:38.710
I want you to be happy, Kuu.

00:05:38.710 --> 00:05:39.890
On that note...

00:05:40.390 --> 00:05:43.500
... may we ask for a portion of the treasure?!

00:05:43.500 --> 00:05:47.140
Spare us a bit, for the sake of Kuu's wedding expenses.

00:05:47.610 --> 00:05:48.970
An opening!

00:05:52.950 --> 00:05:55.650
What's all this?!

00:05:55.650 --> 00:05:58.110
There isn't a single treasure in here!

00:05:58.110 --> 00:05:59.180
Here?

00:05:59.180 --> 00:06:02.120
Hey! Where did you hide the treasure?

00:06:02.120 --> 00:06:04.250
It's been like that the entire time.

00:06:04.250 --> 00:06:08.170
Huh?! Then what are you guys doing here?

00:06:09.590 --> 00:06:11.340
Well, you see, uh...

00:06:11.340 --> 00:06:13.720
H-Heroes' rel—

00:06:15.590 --> 00:06:18.370
We're here under the orders of the King of Imperial Nelpha,

00:06:18.370 --> 00:06:21.690
conducting a secret investigation.

00:06:21.690 --> 00:06:24.890
I see. Then there's no need for us to stick around here.

00:06:24.890 --> 00:06:26.410
Let's go, brother Sui.

00:06:27.880 --> 00:06:29.740
Sorry for the bother!

00:06:35.810 --> 00:06:37.990
Investigators from Nelpha, huh?

00:06:45.720 --> 00:06:47.010
Lear?

00:06:47.010 --> 00:06:50.670
Are you feeling sick? You don't look like you've eaten much.

00:06:50.670 --> 00:06:55.980
Oh, no. It's just that... we haven't had any success at all since coming to this town.

00:06:58.120 --> 00:07:02.130
If only that taboo breaker guy would use some flashy magic,

00:07:02.130 --> 00:07:03.860
we could hear some rumors.

00:07:03.860 --> 00:07:05.460
Do you realize what you're saying?

00:07:05.460 --> 00:07:07.660
If that happened in a different nation,

00:07:07.660 --> 00:07:10.460
wouldn't that lay Roland's magic bare for everyone to see?

00:07:10.460 --> 00:07:14.310
Moo's right. If other countries were to learn the secrets of our magic...

00:07:16.040 --> 00:07:18.810
... it would be tantamount to Roland's downfall.

00:07:18.810 --> 00:07:22.220
That is how dangerous the existence of taboo breakers is.

00:07:22.220 --> 00:07:23.390
Yeah...

00:07:24.060 --> 00:07:26.590
<i>A taboo breaker, who mastered our magic</i>

00:07:26.590 --> 00:07:29.710
<i>and absconded to another land...</i>

00:07:31.080 --> 00:07:36.260
<i>Our taboo breaker pursuit mission is pivotal to the fate of our nation.</i>

00:07:36.260 --> 00:07:38.070
<i>That's why Master Sion directly...</i>

00:07:40.710 --> 00:07:41.910
<i>We'll do our best!</i>

00:07:42.250 --> 00:07:44.400
Leaving aside more complicated matters...

00:07:45.560 --> 00:07:47.270
... how would you like some dessert?

00:07:49.110 --> 00:07:51.750
It looks delicious! Thank you!

00:07:58.800 --> 00:08:00.410
That's great.

00:08:00.410 --> 00:08:03.670
When the Captain has that dreamy expression...!

00:08:12.200 --> 00:08:14.720
Captain? Is something the matter?

00:08:15.020 --> 00:08:17.840
It's because you were mocking her, Lach!

00:08:17.840 --> 00:08:19.720
Hey, you said it first!

00:08:20.970 --> 00:08:25.230
No, no. I'm fine, okay?

00:08:25.230 --> 00:08:31.030
I was so happy that we could all enjoy a nice meal together like this, I just...

00:08:33.120 --> 00:08:35.020
Uhm...

00:08:35.020 --> 00:08:37.740
Please pardon us for interrupting your meal!

00:08:38.500 --> 00:08:41.540
Are you the ones gathering information on taboo breakers?

00:08:41.540 --> 00:08:43.130
Y-Yes.

00:08:43.130 --> 00:08:46.610
We encountered two people who seemed an awful lot like taboo breakers.

00:08:47.400 --> 00:08:49.490
Tell me everything!

00:08:52.810 --> 00:08:53.780
Fiole.

00:08:57.600 --> 00:08:59.660
I'm sorry I took so long to come to this place.

00:09:00.990 --> 00:09:03.300
My power is never enough...

00:09:05.110 --> 00:09:07.060
I keep speaking so conceitedly,

00:09:07.650 --> 00:09:09.020
yet, even now, I can't lay a finger...

00:09:10.150 --> 00:09:12.170
... on the nobles of this land!

00:09:12.170 --> 00:09:15.470
Again... Give up that habit already.

00:09:22.680 --> 00:09:26.900
This is Fiole Folkal's younger sister, Eslina Folkal.

00:09:29.400 --> 00:09:33.000
Please, don't hold such an expression.

00:09:34.470 --> 00:09:36.270
It will sadden my brother.

00:09:38.370 --> 00:09:40.680
My brother was happy.

00:09:41.170 --> 00:09:43.150
He spoke so much of how happy he was...

00:09:44.970 --> 00:09:47.540
... to be of service to His Majesty,

00:09:48.460 --> 00:09:53.280
in the letters... he sent me...

00:10:17.050 --> 00:10:17.960
There he is!

00:10:19.010 --> 00:10:21.640
It's just as the siblings told us.

00:10:21.640 --> 00:10:22.190
Yeah.

00:10:22.770 --> 00:10:27.010
<i>Ryner, that violent twisted woman must be exploiting some weakness of yours,</i>

00:10:27.010 --> 00:10:29.530
<i>using you in all kinds of wicked ploys.</i>

00:10:29.850 --> 00:10:33.350
<i>I am the only one who can save Ryner now!</i>

00:10:36.940 --> 00:10:38.310
<i>And then...!</i>

00:10:44.330 --> 00:10:45.890
Uhm, Captain?

00:10:45.890 --> 00:10:47.150
Yes?

00:10:47.540 --> 00:10:48.570
Your orders?

00:10:48.570 --> 00:10:50.160
Ah, right.

00:10:51.070 --> 00:10:53.670
First, I'll draw their attention with magic.

00:10:53.670 --> 00:10:55.090
Moo, back me up.

00:10:55.090 --> 00:10:56.090
Roger, ma'am.

00:10:56.090 --> 00:10:58.930
Luke, Lach, and Lear, you'll attack with swords.

00:10:58.930 --> 00:11:02.140
Reduce the taboo breaker's combat capabilities and apprehend him.

00:11:02.140 --> 00:11:03.130
Understood.

00:11:03.770 --> 00:11:06.190
Then, commence with the operation!

00:11:06.190 --> 00:11:06.720
Yes!

00:11:09.780 --> 00:11:12.640
<i>Ryner, I'm going to save you now!</i>

00:11:14.290 --> 00:11:17.100
What I seek is thunder! Izuchi!

00:11:27.160 --> 00:11:29.200
There's trouble! Protect the captain!

00:11:54.810 --> 00:11:59.100
So, this girl is an acquaintance of yours?

00:12:03.490 --> 00:12:06.890
No way, you still don't remember? I'm Milk!

00:12:06.890 --> 00:12:10.530
You know, Milk! We were at the same orphanage!

00:12:12.390 --> 00:12:13.380
Who was that again?

00:12:14.620 --> 00:12:16.700
It can't be...

00:12:17.780 --> 00:12:21.640
I can't believe this! And after you even promised to marry me!

00:12:21.640 --> 00:12:22.990
Eh? Marry you?

00:12:22.990 --> 00:12:25.320
Really, you were using marriage as bait

00:12:25.320 --> 00:12:27.530
and devouring young girls at such a young age?

00:12:27.530 --> 00:12:28.730
The hell I did!

00:12:29.060 --> 00:12:34.870
And? If that promise is true, would you want to marry Ryner?

00:12:36.180 --> 00:12:40.370
W-Well... Promise or not,

00:12:40.370 --> 00:12:42.530
it was back when we were kids, I guess...

00:12:42.530 --> 00:12:47.730
Still... To meet again like this, the red threat of fate must be involved...

00:12:47.730 --> 00:12:48.860
Don't you agree?

00:12:48.860 --> 00:12:51.460
And the boy from that day, that you've finally reunited with,

00:12:51.460 --> 00:12:53.880
has grown into an all-time degenerate!

00:12:53.880 --> 00:12:56.060
Yes, a degenerate...

00:12:56.850 --> 00:12:59.730
Hey! Stop making strange interjections!

00:12:59.730 --> 00:13:01.140
This is an act of mercy.

00:13:01.140 --> 00:13:03.870
I'll sever the thread of fate that brings you misfortune,

00:13:03.870 --> 00:13:06.190
along with this man's head.

00:13:06.190 --> 00:13:09.840
No! Ryner, run for it!

00:13:10.200 --> 00:13:11.730
I'm not sticking around for this.

00:13:13.070 --> 00:13:16.530
I suppose if we don't get back to work soon, the day will pass by.

00:13:16.530 --> 00:13:19.020
Hold on, wait a minute!

00:13:19.020 --> 00:13:22.370
Ryner! Ryner!

00:13:25.130 --> 00:13:27.500
If Sion gave them those orders,

00:13:27.500 --> 00:13:29.660
why do I have to be chased around?

00:13:29.660 --> 00:13:31.760
Our search for relics is a top secret mission.

00:13:32.030 --> 00:13:34.820
Instructions concerning us probably haven't spread that far.

00:13:34.820 --> 00:13:36.680
But, still...

00:13:38.230 --> 00:13:39.490
No way!

00:13:46.900 --> 00:13:48.420
It's no use.

00:13:49.500 --> 00:13:51.830
The Alpha Stigma can't get a reading on it.

00:13:51.830 --> 00:13:55.600
There are traces indicating that it's been bestowed with some kind of power, but...

00:14:01.910 --> 00:14:05.200
Yes, that's the spirit! Hang in there, Lach!

00:14:12.380 --> 00:14:15.870
It must be a Nelphan army garrison patrol.

00:14:16.290 --> 00:14:18.940
If we called out loudly, we might get some help.

00:14:18.940 --> 00:14:24.210
Indeed, we do have permission from Nelpha in our pursuit of taboo breakers.

00:14:24.210 --> 00:14:27.180
But if we have to spend time verifying our identities,

00:14:27.180 --> 00:14:28.860
the taboo breaker will get away.

00:14:29.280 --> 00:14:33.920
<i>This is bad... They must be out to capture Ryner!</i>

00:14:35.070 --> 00:14:36.310
<i>I have to protect him.</i>

00:14:36.830 --> 00:14:39.310
Captain Milk...?

00:14:39.640 --> 00:14:44.230
<i>This time... This time... It's my turn to save Ryner!</i>

00:14:44.460 --> 00:14:46.300
<i>For that, I would...</i>

00:14:48.410 --> 00:14:51.380
I-I have to pee!

00:14:52.270 --> 00:14:57.090
Hey! Tying a girl up, have you no shame?!

00:14:57.090 --> 00:15:01.340
Girls have complicated circumstances!

00:15:01.340 --> 00:15:02.300
There they are!

00:15:12.290 --> 00:15:13.870
What's the meaning of this?!

00:15:13.870 --> 00:15:17.060
Just now, that was Roland magic, Izuchi!

00:15:20.710 --> 00:15:22.070
It's Ante.

00:15:22.070 --> 00:15:24.570
A spell which works by stopping vibrations in the air to prevent the transmission of sound.

00:15:24.570 --> 00:15:27.060
A simple spell, but...

00:15:27.400 --> 00:15:29.820
An optimal one for causing disruption on a battlefield.

00:15:36.180 --> 00:15:37.710
What's going on?

00:15:44.330 --> 00:15:45.980
Damn you!

00:15:51.740 --> 00:15:53.800
Ouch...

00:15:55.200 --> 00:15:56.550
You all right?

00:16:00.710 --> 00:16:01.930
Ryner...

00:16:03.850 --> 00:16:07.490
Ryner, you dummy! Why'd you come to save me?!

00:16:07.490 --> 00:16:10.610
I went through all that trouble to give you a chance to run away!

00:16:11.820 --> 00:16:15.170
Jeez, and here I thought I'd saved you.

00:16:15.170 --> 00:16:16.820
Way to burst my bubble.

00:16:16.820 --> 00:16:18.800
Captain, are you all right?

00:16:18.800 --> 00:16:19.800
Ryner!

00:16:20.100 --> 00:16:24.250
If we have to protect the girl you abandoned along with these men,

00:16:24.250 --> 00:16:26.560
I can't guarantee we'll win against these numbers.

00:16:28.160 --> 00:16:29.680
Who abandoned who?!

00:16:29.680 --> 00:16:31.920
You're holding the hero's sword.

00:16:31.920 --> 00:16:34.010
That makes <i>you</i> the hero.

00:16:35.160 --> 00:16:37.640
If you're a hero, do something about this right now.

00:16:38.090 --> 00:16:40.300
What's with that reasoning?

00:16:40.300 --> 00:16:42.820
I don't even know how to make this thing work.

00:16:42.820 --> 00:16:43.920
Find out now.

00:16:43.920 --> 00:16:45.150
For crying out loud...

00:16:48.630 --> 00:16:50.730
I don't get it at all.

00:16:52.400 --> 00:16:54.940
I don't see a thing!

00:16:56.890 --> 00:16:57.990
Well?!

00:16:57.990 --> 00:17:01.830
There's no way I could analyze this thing

00:17:02.580 --> 00:17:04.630
in a situation like this!

00:17:15.470 --> 00:17:16.920
What's happening?

00:17:16.920 --> 00:17:18.470
Ryner! What did you do?

00:17:19.260 --> 00:17:20.750
Who knows?

00:17:44.890 --> 00:17:46.680
R-Retreat!

00:17:51.030 --> 00:17:52.340
Impressive.

00:17:52.620 --> 00:17:54.690
Is that a legendary hero?

00:17:54.690 --> 00:17:56.600
No, it's clearly a dragon.

00:17:56.600 --> 00:18:00.840
Whatever the case, let's put an end to this pointlessly dangerous being.

00:18:00.840 --> 00:18:01.590
How?

00:18:09.770 --> 00:18:11.310
Are you kidding?

00:18:11.310 --> 00:18:13.260
How could you just walk away from the dragon?!

00:18:13.260 --> 00:18:16.750
Hey! You brought it out, you should take care of this!

00:18:16.750 --> 00:18:19.380
Isn't that common sense?!

00:18:26.380 --> 00:18:31.290
I... have no right to be called a captain.

00:18:33.670 --> 00:18:37.690
I mean... I... back there...

00:18:40.610 --> 00:18:42.940
<i>I said that this time, I would be the one to save Ryner.</i>

00:18:43.430 --> 00:18:46.640
<i>For that, I would throw away everything.</i>

00:18:47.140 --> 00:18:51.180
<i>That would mean betraying all of you, whom I greatly care for.</i>

00:18:52.570 --> 00:18:55.620
Captain Milk. Please don't look so sad.

00:18:57.440 --> 00:18:59.170
Do you remember, Captain?

00:18:59.520 --> 00:19:01.820
The day this squadron was formed?

00:19:03.980 --> 00:19:05.740
I, Milk Callaud...

00:19:06.500 --> 00:19:10.460
... humbly accept the mission of pursuing taboo breakers!

00:19:10.460 --> 00:19:11.910
Very good.

00:19:12.570 --> 00:19:17.500
What you are embarking upon is a dirty job, killing those who used to be your brethren.

00:19:17.500 --> 00:19:21.340
In the future, other may use that as a reason to single you out.

00:19:22.080 --> 00:19:24.210
I am grateful for your concern.

00:19:25.210 --> 00:19:28.560
But, I'll accept whatever injury that may occur.

00:19:29.390 --> 00:19:33.850
I once gave up on life.

00:19:34.290 --> 00:19:38.170
I sought to escape my harsh reality, to ease everything.

00:19:47.950 --> 00:19:54.420
But a boy, a childhood friend of mine, gave me the courage to live.

00:19:54.720 --> 00:19:59.760
I want to repay that boy one day.

00:20:00.520 --> 00:20:04.530
And I want to protect Roland, the place where I met him.

00:20:04.530 --> 00:20:05.880
That's why...

00:20:07.700 --> 00:20:11.610
... I shall accept the mission to pursue taboo breakers with pride!

00:20:11.830 --> 00:20:14.790
Back then, we decided.

00:20:16.150 --> 00:20:18.760
We decided to believe in Captain Milk, and to stick with her.

00:20:19.110 --> 00:20:23.870
So, Captain, it's all right for you to assume that you're doing the right thing.

00:20:24.490 --> 00:20:26.200
There's no reason to trouble yourself.

00:20:26.860 --> 00:20:28.930
If you commit an error,

00:20:28.930 --> 00:20:31.710
we'll correct it.

00:20:34.360 --> 00:20:38.050
Whatever happens, we're on your side.

00:20:38.050 --> 00:20:40.210
You are our captain.

00:20:40.210 --> 00:20:44.090
Let's enjoy another fun meal together.

00:20:44.090 --> 00:20:45.310
After all...

00:20:46.540 --> 00:20:47.960
... that's what family does.

00:20:49.310 --> 00:20:50.520
Family...?

00:20:58.770 --> 00:20:59.710
Right!

00:21:02.510 --> 00:21:08.190
It's my fault that Fiole wasn't protected... no, that he was murdered.

00:21:15.570 --> 00:21:19.670
Ever since he met you, Your Majesty, he never stopped talking about you.

00:21:19.670 --> 00:21:20.960
That's why...

00:21:21.430 --> 00:21:25.220
I also wish to be of use to the king who made my brother so happy.

00:21:29.120 --> 00:21:32.580
You're saying you wish to serve me?

00:21:33.470 --> 00:21:34.310
Yes.

00:21:39.340 --> 00:21:40.470
Your Majesty.

00:21:40.470 --> 00:21:43.480
The nobles of Estabul, our vassal state to the east,

00:21:44.110 --> 00:21:45.570
have started a revolt.

00:23:21.190 --> 00:23:24.440
<i>Revolts suck.</i>

00:23:24.440 --> 00:23:26.790
<i>Nations, royalty, ambition, all of it.</i>

00:23:26.790 --> 00:23:28.950
<i>Sion, quit agonizing over every little thing.</i>

00:23:28.950 --> 00:23:32.890
<i>Just tell them, "You're all a hassle!"</i>

00:23:32.890 --> 00:23:35.220
<i>Ah, this is a pain.</i>
